5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Heginbotham</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Abramson</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>MacKinnon</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A functional connection between the pores of distantly related ion channels as revealed by mutant K&#x0002b; channels</article-title><source>Science (Wash DC)</source><year>1992</year><volume>258</volume><fpage>1152</fpage><lpage>1155</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1279807</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="other">Hille, B. 1992. Ionic Channels of Excitable Membranes. Sinauer Associates Inc., Sunderland, MA.</citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ildefonse</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Crouzy</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bennett</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gating of retinal rod cation channel by different nucleotides: comparative study of unitary currents</article-title><source>J Membr Biol</source><year>1992</year><volume>130</volume><fpage>91</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1281886</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jan</surname><given-names>LY</given-names></name><name><surname>Jan</surname><given-names>YN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A superfamily of ion channels</article-title><source>Nature  (Lond)</source><year>1990</year><volume>345</volume><fpage>672</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1694264</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karpen</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Stryer</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Baylor</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Interactions between divalent cations and the gating machinery of cyclic GMP&#x02013;activated channels in salamander retinal rods</article-title><source>J Gen Physiol</source><year>1993</year><volume>101</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>25</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7679715</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kaupp</surname><given-names>UB</given-names></name><name><surname>Niidome</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Tanabe</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Terada</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonigk</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Stuhmer</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Kangawa</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Matsuo</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Hirose</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Primary structure and functional expression from complementary DNA of the rod photoreceptor cyclic GMP-gated channel</article-title><source>Nature (Lond)</source><year>1989</year><volume>342</volume><fpage>762</fpage><lpage>766</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2481236</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lancet</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Vertebrate olfactory reception</article-title><source>Annu Rev Neurosci</source><year>1986</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>329</fpage><lpage>355</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2423007</pub-